# Pairs with ScopelessToolsClusterWide. The MCP telemetry handler accepts the
# caller's Telemetry grant over its validated active tenant's capability
# scope, so a tenant-confined grant (#5582) runs a raw PromQL expression that
# cannot be pinned to that tenant.
MODULE: TelemetryHonoursTenantCapability
TARGET: ScopelessToolsClusterWide
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the MCP telemetry handler falls back to the active tenant's capability scope
PERTURBS: CallGroupTool

--- FIND
        fac == IF t = "telemetry" THEN AllowedUnder(policy, c, "Telemetry", ClusterTelemetry) ELSE
--- REPLACE
        fac == IF t = "telemetry" THEN AllowedUnder(policy, c, "Telemetry", ClusterTelemetry) \/ (Resolve(c, session.hdr) # NoTenant /\ AllowedUnder(policy, c, "Telemetry", Scope(TenantCapability(Resolve(c, session.hdr)), NoKey))) ELSE
--- END
